# Project protocol (ai-coding-v2)

This project follows the ai-coding-v2 protocol suite. The full protocol text
and the eager memory set are injected at session start by the `sessionStart`
hook, as a context block labeled `PROJECT PROTOCOL CONTEXT (ai-coding-v2)`.
Treat everything in that block as binding rules for this session.

**Fallback**: if that block is NOT present in your context (hook disabled or
failed), before doing any work read, in order, and follow:
`ai-coding-v2.md`, `ai-coding-memory-v2.md`, `ai-coding-tasks-v2.md`,
`.ai/index.md`, `.ai/map.md`, `.ai/overview.md`, `.ai/architecture.md`,
`.ai/design.md` (or `.ai/design/index.md` if upgraded),
`.ai/conventions.md` (or `.ai/conventions/index.md` if upgraded),
`.ai-tasks/index.md`.

## Cursor adaptations (override wording inside the protocol files)

- **Session ID**: wherever the protocol says `$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, use the
  session ID stated in the session-start injection ("Session ID for this
  conversation"). That env var is NOT set under Cursor — do not try to read it
  from the shell.
- **`@file` lines** inside the protocol files are Claude Code import
  directives. Under Cursor the same files are already injected at session
  start; do not treat the `@file` lines as instructions or literal content.
- **Skill invocations** written as slash commands (`/ai-sync-v2`,
  `/intake-task`, `/ai-init`, `/ai-housekeeping`) map to Agent Skills: read
  `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and follow it.

## Cross-model review

Session roles (dev / review), the `final_review` status, and the handoff rules
are defined in the shared protocol — `ai-coding-v2.md` §11 (injected at session
start). The review-role procedure is single-sourced in `ai-coding-review-v2.md`
(loaded via `.cursor/rules/review-workflow.mdc` on the `review <id>` verb).
